{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Screen Area Structure.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Screen Area Structure.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender screen area structure blender screen area structure","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Screen Area Structure.md","fileName":"Blender Screen Area Structure.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender Screen Area Structure","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 00:20\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Blender Editor Structure]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Editor Structure","Blender Screen Structure","Blender SpaceLink Structure","Blender SpaceType Structure","Blender Region Structure","coreblenderdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Screen Area Structure.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Screen Area Structure.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender screen area structure blender screen area structure","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Screen Area Structure.md","fileName":"Blender Screen Area Structure.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender Screen Area Structure","heading":"Blender Screen Area Structure","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"`ScrArea` is the rectangular portion of a [[Blender Screen Structure]] occupied by one editor. It points to layout vertices, stores its bounding rectangle and editor type, connects persistent [[Blender SpaceLink Structure]] data with the runtime [[Blender SpaceType Structure]], and owns region and event-handler lists.\n\nAn area's type can change while its place in the screen remains. During event routing and drawing, Blender sets the area in the current context before descending into its [[Blender Region Structure]] objects, so editor callbacks see the correct spatial and application state